---
What a shop charges to deliver a basket. Pure code in a commons: the kind of
small rule a test can pass over without pinning down, which is what
`bynk test --mutate` finds out.
---
commons shop.delivery

--- A basket worth this much, in pence, or more ships free.
const FreeFrom: Int = 5000

--- What delivery costs, in pence, below [FreeFrom].
const Standard: Int = 399

---
The delivery charge, in pence. Members never pay it, and nor does a basket
worth [FreeFrom] or more.
---
fn charge(basket: Int, member: Bool) -> Int {
	if member || basket >= FreeFrom { 0 } else { Standard }
}

--- What the customer pays, in pence: the basket plus its delivery.
fn total(basket: Int, member: Bool) -> Int {
	basket + charge(basket, member)
}
